  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37143114",
      "title": "Working with \"Futures\" for Handling Data from the Future",
      "lectureOrder": 115,
      "videoOrder": 106,
      "sourceHash": "f7ba234d83d52faa9ff973ac3108d4dd17e2f4d53097adc3123cdfef08b5df53",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.63,
          "en": "So, how can we now store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.63,
          "end": 5.673,
          "en": "that date that was selected?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.63,
          "end": 11.63,
          "en": "Well, showDatePicker in the end returns that picked date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "but wrapped into a so-called future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 17.73,
          "en": "a value of type Future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.73,
          "end": 20.76,
          "en": "which we haven't encountered thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.76,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "Now, futures are a very important data type built into Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 28.32,
          "en": "You will see futures again later in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.32,
          "end": 31.02,
          "en": "when we work with HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.02,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "and the future simply is an object from the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.44,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 38.34,
          "en": "It simply is an object that wraps a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.34,
          "end": 40.35,
          "en": "which you don't have yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.35,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "but which you will have in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 45.15,
          "en": "Like here for showDatePicker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.15,
          "end": 47.79,
          "en": "when this line of code is executed by Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 50.823,
          "en": "it opens this date picker and shows it on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.38,
          "end": 55.92,
          "en": "But of course, no date has been picked yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "That will only happen in the future, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 61.38,
          "en": "Therefore, Flutter internally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.38,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "basically memorizes that in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 66.75,
          "en": "some value will be picked here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.75,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "and it allows you to register a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 72.57,
          "en": "that should be executed in that future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.57,
          "end": 75.21000000000001,
          "en": "once that value is available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.21000000000001,
          "end": 77.85,
          "en": "And that function can be registered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.85,
          "end": 80.76,
          "en": "by calling a method on that object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.76,
          "end": 85.08,
          "en": "on that future object that is returned by showDatePicker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.08,
          "end": 86.49,
          "en": "So, this future object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 88.28999999999999,
          "en": "and that's important to understand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 90.03,
          "en": "is returned immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.03,
          "end": 92.91,
          "en": "but it doesn't contain the picked value yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 96.27000000000001,
          "en": "Instead, this future object gives you a then method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 97.56,
          "en": "which you can call,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.56,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "to which you can pass a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "an anonymous function, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.85,
          "en": "which then will get that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.85,
          "end": 106.74000000000001,
          "en": "which in this case here has been picked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "once it has been picked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "So this function which you pass to then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "will be executed by Flutter once the value is available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "so once a date has been picked here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "It's kind of similar to how buttons work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "where we also define a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 126.21,
          "en": "that will be executed in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.21,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "but here we're dealing with a widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "where we set this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 134.31,
          "en": "as a value for one of the many widget arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.31,
          "end": 135.783,
          "en": "In case of showDatePicker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 138.96,
          "en": "we instead get such a future object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 141.12,
          "en": "to which we pass such a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.12,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "but the idea is generally the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 147.27,
          "en": "that we wanna get hold of some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.27,
          "end": 149.853,
          "en": "or some event in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 153,
          "en": "Now, using such a then method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153,
          "end": 155.61,
          "en": "is a one way of getting hold of that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 157.38,
          "en": "A more convenient method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 160.41,
          "en": "is to add the special async keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.41,
          "end": 164.79,
          "en": "here between the parentheses after the method name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 164.79,
          "end": 168.24,
          "en": "before the opening curly brace,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 168.24,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "and then add the await keyword in front of the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 174.873,
          "en": "that does yield such a future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.74,
          "end": 178.92000000000002,
          "en": "So you can't use async await here in the build method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 178.92000000000002,
          "end": 180.27,
          "en": "for your widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.27,
          "end": 181.35,
          "en": "but you can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 181.35,
          "end": 184.173,
          "en": "whenever you get such a future value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 185.22,
          "end": 187.53,
          "en": "If you use await here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 187.53,
          "end": 191.67,
          "en": "you get access to that pickedDate in this case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.67,
          "end": 194.73,
          "en": "as a value in a regular variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 194.73,
          "end": 197.79,
          "en": "But even though this now looks like all the other code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 197.79,
          "end": 200.34,
          "en": "or almost like all the other code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 200.34,
          "end": 204.63,
          "en": "the await keyword internally simply tells Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 204.63,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "that this value that should be stored in pickedDate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 210.27,
          "en": "won't be available immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 210.27,
          "end": 212.57999999999998,
          "en": "but at least at some point in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 212.57999999999998,
          "end": 217.26,
          "en": "and Flutter should therefore basically wait for that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 219.933,
          "en": "before it stores it in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 223.2,
          "en": "Nonetheless, Flutter will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 223.2,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "that the next line after this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 227.82,
          "en": "so this line here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 227.82,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "will only be executed once the value is available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 235.44,
          "en": "So it will really kind of wait for that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 235.44,
          "end": 238.473,
          "en": "and therefore here we could print that pickedDate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.55,
          "end": 241.83,
          "en": "or we could store it in a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 241.83,
          "end": 244.23,
          "en": "possibly even with setState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 244.23,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "so that we could output it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 248.733,
          "en": "in this Text next to this IconButton.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 249.69,
          "end": 252.42,
          "en": "And that is indeed what I wanna do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 252.42,
          "end": 254.793,
          "en": "So I'll add a new variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 255.84,
          "end": 258.51,
          "en": "_selectedDate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 258.51,
          "end": 261.09,
          "en": "which should be of type DateTime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 261.09,
          "end": 263.16,
          "en": "And since I am setting a type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 263.16,
          "end": 265.413,
          "en": "the var keyword must be omitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 266.31,
          "end": 269.85,
          "en": "And actually it initially will not hold a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 269.85,
          "end": 273.36,
          "en": "hence it should be DateTime? to tell Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.36,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "that selectedDate either stores a value of type DateTime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 282.15,
          "en": "or nothing, null as it's called in Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.15,
          "end": 284.28,
          "en": "And instead of _presentDatePicker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 284.28,
          "end": 287.67,
          "en": "here after waiting for the _selectedDate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 287.67,
          "end": 289.09000000000003,
          "en": "we can call setState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 290.88,
          "end": 293.763,
          "en": "and set _selectedDate = pickedDate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 296.751,
          "end": 299.55,
          "en": "And pickedDate is of type DateTime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 299.55,
          "end": 301.593,
          "en": "so setting it like this is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 303.51,
          "end": 306.54,
          "en": "And with that, we can use this _selectedDate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 306.54,
          "end": 308.91,
          "en": "to output it down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.91,
          "end": 311.31,
          "en": "Of course, here I again want to output a version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 311.31,
          "end": 313.23,
          "en": "that's human readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 313.23,
          "end": 314.52,
          "en": "And for that reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.52,
          "end": 316.92,
          "en": "I'll use the same approach I used before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 316.92,
          "end": 318.52,
          "en": "in my expense model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 319.95,
          "end": 321.9,
          "en": "where I use this intel package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 321.9,
          "end": 324.09,
          "en": "and such a formatter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 324.09,
          "end": 325.14,
          "en": "by adding it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 325.14,
          "end": 328.29,
          "en": "to this new_expense.dart file as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 331.743,
          "en": "And this formatter can be set up outside of any class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 333.3,
          "end": 337.98,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could of course also simply import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 337.98,
          "end": 340.56,
          "en": "from our own package here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 340.56,
          "end": 342.81,
          "en": "So from our own project package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 342.81,
          "end": 346.5,
          "en": "and there from the expense.dart file in the models folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 346.5,
          "end": 349.08,
          "en": "because in there we set up this formatter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 349.08,
          "end": 350.76,
          "en": "so it is actually available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 350.76,
          "end": 352.923,
          "en": "as soon as we import from this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 354,
          "end": 357.45,
          "en": "And we can use this formatter down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 357.45,
          "end": 360.51,
          "en": "to not output _selectedDate here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 360.51,
          "end": 362.85,
          "en": "but instead, I want to output No date selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 362.85,
          "end": 365.13,
          "en": "if we haven't selected a date yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 365.13,
          "end": 367.72,
          "en": "so I want to check if _selectedDate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 369.33,
          "end": 370.833,
          "en": "is equal to null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 371.67,
          "end": 374.19,
          "en": "and then we can use a ternary expression here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 374.19,
          "end": 377.043,
          "en": "to output No date selected in that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 378.18,
          "end": 382.15,
          "en": "Or alternatively, we can use the formatter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 383.28,
          "end": 386.4,
          "en": "and call format on the _selectedDate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 386.4,
          "end": 389.52,
          "en": "to output a formatted version of that date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 389.52,
          "end": 391.97,
          "en": "and now we have to remove the const keyword here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
